  <section class="section bg-surface-muted">
    <Container variant="narrow">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>How Client-Side Image Conversion Works</h2>
        <p>
          QuickJPG runs directly inside your web browser using the HTML5 Canvas API and WebAssembly decoders. When you select a photo, document, or graphic, your device reads the file into local memory, decodes its pixel buffer, and re-encodes it into your target format without transmitting bytes over the network.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because processing stays on your hardware, conversion speed scales with your CPU and finishes without server upload queues, bandwidth caps, or temporary cloud storage retention.
        </p>

        <h3>Choosing the Right Image Format</h3>
        <p>
          Different file formats optimize for different priorities—file weight, lossless edges, transparency, or universal compatibility across operating systems and portals.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong><a href="/jpg-to-png/">JPG to PNG</a></strong> — Useful when you need lossless storage, sharp screenshots, crisp UI text, or transparent backgrounds via alpha editing.</li>
          <li><strong><a href="/png-to-jpg/">PNG to JPG</a></strong> — Reduces photograph file size dramatically by discarding unneeded alpha channels and applying perceptual chroma subsampling.</li>
          <li><strong><a href="/jpg-to-webp/">JPG to WebP</a></strong> — Typically delivers 25–35% smaller web assets at comparable visual fidelity, improving Core Web Vitals (LCP).</li>
          <li><strong><a href="/webp-to-jpg/">WebP to JPG</a></strong> — Ensures compatibility with legacy photo editors, desktop viewers, and strict upload portals.</li>
          <li><strong><a href="/jpg-to-pdf/">JPG to PDF</a></strong> — Bundles single or multiple scanned pages and receipts into a standardized document container.</li>
          <li><strong><a href="/heic-to-jpg/">HEIC to JPG</a></strong> — Converts Apple High Efficiency Image Container files from iPhone and iPad cameras into broadly readable JPEGs.</li>
          <li><strong><a href="/resize-jpg/">Resize JPG</a></strong> — Scales image dimensions accurately before publishing to social platforms or product catalogs.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Compression, Dimensions, and Upload Requirements</h3>
        <p>
          Most government application portals, visa systems, and job forms enforce strict byte ceilings (such as 20KB, 50KB, or 100KB) alongside exact pixel dimensions. Instead of guessing export sliders repeatedly, our specialized sizing utilities adjust encoding quality iteratively until the output meets your target budget while preserving legibility.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong><a href="/passport-photo-size/">Passport Photo Size</a></strong> — Crop and dimension portraits cleanly for country-specific official photo specifications.</li>
          <li><strong><a href="/compress-for-govt-form/">Compress for Govt Form</a></strong> — Target exact KB limits such as 20KB, 50KB, or 100KB for exam and civil portal uploads.</li>
          <li><strong><a href="/photo-to-base64/">Photo to Base64</a></strong> — Generate inline data URIs and Base64 payloads for HTML, CSS, and frontend bundles.</li>
          <li><strong><a href="/compress-to-100kb/">Compress to 100KB</a></strong> — Optimize high-resolution photos down below 100KB with selectable quality presets.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

